# AWS Scripts Reorganization - June 2025

## What Was Done

Reorganized the `/infra/aws/` directory from a flat structure to a categorized, maintainable structure.

## Before (Flat Structure)
```
aws/
├── deploy-monitoring-to-existing.sh
├── setup-ssl-monitoring.sh
├── deploy-monitoring-one-click.sh
├── check-environment.sh
├── fix-grafana-subpath.sh
├── DOCKER_NETWORKING_FIX.md
├── add-loki-integration.sh
└── open-monitoring-ports.sh
```

## After (Organized Structure)
```
aws/
├── aws-helper.sh              # NEW: Interactive menu
├── README.md                  # NEW: Comprehensive documentation
├── deployment/                # Main deployment scripts
│   ├── deploy-monitoring-one-click.sh
│   └── deploy-monitoring-to-existing.sh
├── setup/                     # Environment and configuration
│   ├── check-environment.sh
│   ├── open-monitoring-ports.sh
│   └── setup-ssl-monitoring.sh
├── monitoring/                # Monitoring utilities
│   └── add-loki-integration.sh
├── troubleshooting/           # Fix and diagnostic scripts
│   └── fix-grafana-subpath.sh
└── docs/                      # Documentation
    └── DOCKER_NETWORKING_FIX.md
```

## Key Improvements

1. **Categorized Organization**: Scripts grouped by purpose
2. **Interactive Helper**: `aws-helper.sh` provides easy access to all functions
3. **Comprehensive Documentation**: Detailed README with usage examples
4. **Fixed Script References**: Updated path references in orchestrator scripts
5. **Better Maintainability**: Clear separation of concerns

## Usage

Instead of remembering script names, users can now:
```bash
./aws-helper.sh
```

This provides an interactive menu for all AWS operations.
